      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T11:09:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After a local discussion with Nicolas, I agree that UseArtImage can be dropped, as jitzygote will be used only as a fallback solution after an ART module update (when the ART boot image changes and there\u0027s a need to run dexopt anyway).\n\nAs a result of dropping UseArtImage, first boot in jitzygote builds will be slow (I\u0027d expect ~2x slower) due to discarding all dexpreopted code and running dexopt. This will affect our CI, but not any real-world scenario, so it\u0027s ok to have if it simplifies the code.\n\nWe will probably have to keep DEXPREOPT_USE_APEX_IMAGE though, as it is needed used in the makefiles to copy the ART image in the place expected by system property dalvik.vm.boot-image in jitzygote builds (see ag/7530804). This needs to be investigated, eg maybe we can set: \n\n  dalvik.vm.boot-image\u003d/apex/com.android.art/javalib/boot.art\n\n... in jitzygote builds and drop DEXPREOPT_USE_APEX_IMAGE altogether.",
      "parentUuid": "8b9326b4_9142dbac",
      "revId": "40139d6422114672770fc9051c346f8f1aba79d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
